the california and san francisco  departments of public health  and the cdc have confirmed  that a recent case of covert 19  among an individual in california was  caused by the omicron variant the  omicron variant has been detected in the  u.s health officials say the patient  recently returned from south africa  where scientists first identified the  variant in november covet cases in the  u.s were already increasing since late  october and we're averaging more than 90  000 a day before thanksgiving when  millions of people traveled to gather  with family and friends hospitalizations  have been creeping upwards as well even  before the variant was confirmed in the  u.s the cdc strengthened its booster  recommendation saying that everybody 18  and older should get a booster shot  we've also seen some tighter travel  restrictions and mask advisories in  places like new york  there's still a lot about the variant  that we don't know  with the small number of cases it is  very difficult to know whether or not  this particular variant is going to  result in severe disease researchers are  concerned about the variant because of  its high numbers of mutations some of  which have already been linked to higher  transmissibility or a partial evasion of  the immune response from vaccination or  prior infection with other variants  president biden son monday that his  administration was working with pfizer  moderna and johnson johnson on plans for  vaccines or boosters in case they're  needed to combat the variant but mr  biden said that as of now officials  don't think such measures will be needed  i will also direct the fda and the cdc  to use the fastest process available  without cutting any corners for safety  to get such vaccines approved and on the  market if needed health officials and  infectious disease experts were already  anticipating an increased number of  coveted cases and hospitalizations this  winter as colder weather ushers people  in many parts of the country indoors and  people gather together for the holidays  public health officials say that the  things that we've been doing all along  to help protect ourselves against other  variants including delta which is most  of the cases in the country right now  can also help against omicron  cdc continues to recommend wearing a  mask in public indoor settings in these  areas  washing your hands frequently and  physical distancing we don't know a lot  about this variant right now but  researchers across the world are working  on it and we should have more answers in  the next couple of weeks
 

